{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power","id":583747,"title":"[Beast] BDSM & the Hunger for Power?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-08T12:39:07-07:00","id":583747,"title":"[Beast] BDSM & the Hunger for Power?","content":"So I was batting around a character idea and stumbled on a thought.<br /> <br /> If a Beast with a Hunger for Power is a professional Dominatrix or into the BDSM scene, would that feed the Horror's Hunger? Would safewords and healthy practices render/impose a penalty to the Satiety roll? Could Satiety even be gained this way at all? For clarity, I am <i>not</i> interested in a Beast with a Hunger for Power expressing their hunger through sexual predation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:42:44-07:00","id":583768,"title":"","content":"I would say it doesn't count. BDSM is largely about the freedom born from trust, where as feeding Satiety is more about putting the fear of the world into someone. It's about breaking down the feeling of safety.<br /> <br /> That line of fear and trust is a dangerous line to walk, and a lot of people can't walk it at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T14:03:02-07:00","id":583826,"title":"","content":"In a healthy/safe BDSM relationship, the Dom/me has very little of the actual power in the relationship, because what does and does not happen in a given scene is pretty much down to what their sub is into. Without making a huge BDSM 101 post, the short version is that I would say it's impossible to feed the Hunger for Power this way. Look to the guiding principle in the book: for someone to eat, something gets eaten. If you aren't harming someone, you aren't getting anything out of it.<br /> <br /> That said, there's an unfortunate number of <i>un</i>healthy BDSM relationships out there, and the more abusive and generally screwed up it gets the closer to feeding you are. Christian 50-Shades-of-terrible-book Grey would be able to feed the Hunger for Power just fine, because his relationship would be like a blood doll without fangs. Obviously every group is comfortable with different things, but for a situation bad enough that I'd consider it feeding-worthy it would be well past the limit of what I'd be comfortable with in most cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:20:14-07:00","id":583903,"title":"","content":"Yeah, BDSM may involve power <i>play</i>, but it's just that, playing. When done safely, all participants should be equal partners, just like in any healthy relationship or sexual encounter. If there is a genuine power imbalance, it's probably not healthy and may be abusive. A Tyrant certainly could feed their hunger for power through unhealthy power dynamics in sexual relationships - there are, unfortunately, a lot of abusers who prey on inexperienced people looking to get involved in the BDSM community and don't know the abusive behavior isn't normal. This problem is made worse by things like the above mentioned terrible book depicting abuse and treating it like it's not only normal behavior in the BDSM community, but that it's somehow romantic. But it sounds like you're more interested in a character who practices healthy, responsible BDSM, which involves full consent and safety measures. If it's being done right, I would say it's not going to satisfy a hunger for power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:50:18-07:00","id":583942,"title":"","content":"As a counter to 50 Shades of Nope, I suggest taking a look at Sunstone, its a Web Comic and Graphic novel about a dom and sub that fall in love. It explores the BDSM world in a very healthy way and even touches on the misconceptions that people have about it. It's very, very good and also very, very NSFW!<br /> <br /> First volume on amazon:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Sunstone-Volume-OGN-Stjepan-Sejic/dp/1632152126\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Sunstone-Volume-OGN-Stjepan-Sejic/dp/1632152126\" target=\"_blank\"> Amazon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Sunstone-Volume-OGN-Stjepan-Sejic/dp/1632152126\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.amazon.com/Sunstone-Volume-OGN-Stjepan-Sejic/dp/1632152126 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> And to Mechalith's point, it might be an interesting concept to have a Tyrant that is actually a sub and feeds from the power of control over the Dom. Still not exactly healthy, but a interesting play on the idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T16:11:52-07:00","id":583963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>indarkestknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power#post583747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was batting around a character idea and stumbled on a thought.<br /> <br /> If a Beast with a Hunger for Power is a professional Dominatrix or into the BDSM scene, would that feed the Horror's Hunger? Would safewords and healthy practices render/impose a penalty to the Satiety roll? Could Satiety even be gained this way at all? For clarity, I am <i>not</i> interested in a Beast with a Hunger for Power expressing their hunger through sexual predation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say that I would ever be comfortable with that character concept at my table, but, if the &quot;corporate ladder-climber&quot; Tyrant is anything to go by, it's not a nonviable concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T16:15:42-07:00","id":583968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=583942#post583942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a counter to 50 Shades of Nope, I suggest taking a look at Sunstone, its a Web Comic and Graphic novel about a dom and sub that fall in love. It explores the BDSM world in a very healthy way and even touches on the misconceptions that people have about it. It's very, very good and also very, very NSFW!<br /> <br /> First volume on amazon:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Sunstone-Volume-OGN-Stjepan-Sejic/dp/1632152126\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.amazon.com/Sunstone-Volum.../dp/1632152126</a><br /> <br /> <br /> And to Mechalith's point, it might be an interesting concept to have a Tyrant that is actually a sub and feeds from the power of control over the Dom. Still not exactly healthy, but a interesting play on the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will unreservedly second ElvesofZion's recommendation re: Sunstone. It's a lovely comic in addition to being a much healthier and more accurate depiction of the subject. I usually recommend it to people, but it didn't seem directly germane to my post so I left it out.<br /> <br /> Oh, and because Hexmeister Vic touched on it as well: to be clear, it isn't the Dominatrix part of the concept I'd have reservations about. It's the degree of abuse and intensely dubious consent that I feel it would have to involve to count as a Hunger. Even off-camera, I don't really want to be playing with a character who sexually abuses or rapes people on a regular basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":1647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","user":"Mechalith","date":". 07-08-2015, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T16:22:31-07:00","id":583974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=583968#post583968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I will unreservedly second ElvesofZion's recommendation re: Sunstone. It's a lovely comic in addition to being a much healthier and more accurate depiction of the subject. I usually recommend it to people, but it didn't seem directly germane to my post so I left it out.<br /> <br /> Oh, and because Hexmeister Vic touched on it as well: to be clear, it isn't the Dominatrix part of the concept I'd have reservations about. It's the degree of abuse and intensely dubious consent that I feel it would have to involve to count as a Hunger. Even off-camera, I don't really want to be playing with a character who sexually abuses or rapes people on a regular basis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course, yeah, you gotta make sure that that is something your group is comfortable with having at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T17:24:57-07:00","id":583997,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your input, everyone. I guess it's back to the drawing board. I'd rather come up with other ways to express Hungers than play a sexual predator or someone who abuses BDSM relationships (coughChristianGreycough).<br /> <br /> Thank you especially to Mechalith and ElvesofZion for the Sunstone recommendation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T22:35:07-07:00","id":584233,"title":"","content":"<b>Short Answer: </b>It only counts towards Hunger if the BDSM relationship is unhealthy and abusive.<br /> Which a few are, and that can be a difficult discussion to have at a table in a mature manner.<br /> Beast touches on some of the darkest subject matter since Blood Bonds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T04:01:04-07:00","id":584497,"title":"","content":"Well, I'de say it depends on whom the character has found to practise it with.<br /> If your character has found a really disturbed person, who enjoys actually being seriously and violently abused, well beyond the point of normal BDSM, I'de think it could feed you, with a slight penalty or something.<br /> I'de also think that that kind of behavior might be a slippery slope for your characters moral compass. Maybe one day he doesn't give a shit about 'safewords' anymore? &quot;Nothing is 'safe' from the BEAST!! *Commence Eldritch tantrum* &quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think being &quot;ok&quot; with depicting rape and rape-ey circumstances depend largely on how its done. I'm part of a few games in which the PC's often engage in horrific actions, but the thrust of those games are that we're all very well aware the PC's aren't the &quot;good guys&quot; or &quot;the heroes&quot;. None of us are under any illusion that those actions are laudable or excuseable. Those games have a sort of &quot;for the greater good&quot; narrative going, which allows us to explore the rationale behind those horrific actions, and how they might concievably be justified, to an abselute lunatic.<br /> Its all about frameing, when depicting that kind of horrific actions. You want to have a <i>reason why </i>the character is acting the way he is, and then explore that reason. Cudos to you, if you can make a downright sympathetic rapist, although I doubt it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That said, you might not wanna do this, if you're playing with somebody who has experienced sexual assault firsthand. Or else, check with that person first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:09:40-07:00","id":584596,"title":"","content":"You know, here's something I think.<br /> <br /> We're talking about satisfying different hungers and cravings. BDSM, despite it being predicated around roleplaying, is a culture that is designed around feeding and exploring various kinds of desires one might have in a safe, sane, and consensual environment.<br /> <br /> Believe it or not, I think that a healthy BDSM relationship it would count. Even if its just play, this relationship still fulfills certain needs people have. And Hunger / Satiety is just taking those ambitions and needs to a supernatural level.<br /> <br /> An established relationship probably wouldn't be worth much in terms of Satiety, and probably only good for feeding at low Satiety (seriously, medium and high feeding requirements are insane!), but I would say its entirely viable.<br /> <br /> What everything said by others still holds true for the most part - I just think that role play should count for feeding Hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:27:09-07:00","id":584616,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I guess. But you dont think it would take the supernatural sting away from the Hunger, if it could be satisfied with a benign relationship?<br /> I think that kinda takes the Horror out of Gothic-Horror. Kinda like if a Vampire could feed his blood-thing by eating a really red steak or if a Prometheans Disquiet just made him really socially awkward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T07:26:47-07:00","id":584721,"title":"","content":"Personally I think it's a great concept. That said, I would agree with the comments above that just average BDSM play would not sate the Hunger. However, I would argue that this could be likened unto an amuse-bouche. While it doesn't sate anything, it does give the Beast a taste of what it desires before the actual meal. Perhaps the person doesn't follow normal community guidelines and is known for ignoring safewords and engaging in really edgy play. It isn't uncommon for someone like that to become involved in the local community. But perhaps the Beast manages to keep the Hunger in check for the most part and when the small appetizer isn't nearly enough they go out and find more elsewhere. There are some ways to keep this concept I think and just push edges of that box out a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751","name":"aslan751","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T07:40:47-07:00","id":584728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=584596#post584596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, here's something I think.<br /> <br /> We're talking about satisfying different hungers and cravings. BDSM, despite it being predicated around roleplaying, is a culture that is designed around feeding and exploring various kinds of desires one might have in a safe, sane, and consensual environment.<br /> <br /> Believe it or not, I think that a healthy BDSM relationship it would count. Even if its just play, this relationship still fulfills certain needs people have. And Hunger / Satiety is just taking those ambitions and needs to a supernatural level.<br /> <br /> An established relationship probably wouldn't be worth much in terms of Satiety, and probably only good for feeding at low Satiety (seriously, medium and high feeding requirements are insane!), but I would say its entirely viable.<br /> <br /> What everything said by others still holds true for the most part - I just think that role play should count for feeding Hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree. Should a Nemisis be able to satisfy her hunger by roleplaying punishing someone? What about a Predator roleplaying a hunt? Or a Collector pretending to hoard things?<br /> <br /> While BDSM may satisfy human needs for certain sensations or power dynamics, I don't see it working for a Tyrant's hunger for power because all partners have power and control over the scene at all times. That may be enough to satisfy a human's need for dominance or submission, but a primordial horror? I don't think it would settle for pretend power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:05:04-07:00","id":584743,"title":"","content":"The primordial horror wants to <i>actually dominate someone</i>. BDSM is about consensual power play. They only look kinda sorta similar from a distance, but are completely different animals up close, and the consent issue is an ugly one that renders actual BDSM not really tenable as a way to feed a Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:39:49-07:00","id":584831,"title":"","content":"You can sate Hoard at low levels by being an ebay shark, or by buying things from a pawn shop, which isn't really hurting anyone or taking something away from them. You can satisfy Punishment at low levels by telling someone off verbally. You can satisfy Prey at low levels by putting yourself in a position where you could attack someone, without them ever knowing you've done it. So, yes, I think ethical BDSM would good for power at low levels (but not higher ones).<br /> <br /> I can't remember who, but someone suggested BDSM as a meal for Ruin based on dispelling limits the partner thinks they have but don't actually have (ie, it only works if they find they're into it).<br /> <br /> The ick factor lingers, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:51:59-07:00","id":584845,"title":"","content":"Verbally telling someone off or sharking stuff off ebay are all genuine activities, but honest to goodness, the power play in BDSM is basically fakery, and that lack of<i> real </i>dominance, however low level it is, would keep it from being satisfying.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm trying to suggest (or clarify? Who knows.) is that if they're engaging in BDSM to satisfy their Hunger, even if it doesn't do long lasting harm it's probably gonna be what we'd call &quot;bad BDSM&quot; because it'll be about <i>actual </i>domination and not power play. It's the commonly cited difference between Christian Grey's legitimately abusive behavior and actual BDSM. It <i>looks </i>like BDSM and <i>sounds </i>like it, but the consensual elements are weak, coerced and there's an underlying level of control that violates the appropriate power dynamic of a relationship.<br /> <br /> Basically, I don't think you're gonna get away with BDSM without it being a bit ugly. If you're cool with that in your game, or you're actually trying to examine that and incorporate it as a character conflict, that sounds interesting, but it might not be super comfortable with people at your average table, especially if they've had any bad experiences. It <i>could </i>be interesting, just try to be mindful of the subject matter and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:06:54-07:00","id":584854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=584845#post584845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Verbally telling someone off or sharking stuff off ebay are all genuine activities, but honest to goodness, the power play in BDSM is basically fakery, and that lack of<i> real </i>dominance, however low level it is, would keep it from being satisfying.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm trying to suggest (or clarify? Who knows.) is that if they're engaging in BDSM to satisfy their Hunger, even if it doesn't do long lasting harm it's probably gonna be what we'd call &amp;quot;bad BDSM&amp;quot; because it'll be about <i>actual </i>domination and not power play. It's the commonly cited difference between Christian Grey's legitimately abusive behavior and actual BDSM. It <i>looks </i>like BDSM and <i>sounds </i>like it, but the consensual elements are weak, coerced and there's an underlying level of control that violates the appropriate power dynamic of a relationship.<br /> <br /> Basically, I don't think you're gonna get away with BDSM without it being a bit ugly. If you're cool with that in your game, or you're actually trying to examine that and incorporate it as a character conflict, that sounds interesting, but it might not be super comfortable with people at your average table, especially if they've had any bad experiences. It <i>could </i>be interesting, just try to be mindful of the subject matter and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, it could be pretty offensive to people who are actually into healthy BDSM. As with everything squicku, just check with the rest of the group, make sure they're cool with it first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:20:24-07:00","id":584860,"title":"","content":"Worth pointing out that the &quot;buy stuff from a jewelry shop&quot; option has been cut down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:40:44-07:00","id":584869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=584845#post584845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess what I'm trying to suggest (or clarify? Who knows.) is that if they're engaging in BDSM to satisfy their Hunger, even if it doesn't do long lasting harm it's probably gonna be what we'd call &quot;bad BDSM&quot; because it'll be about <i>actual </i>domination and not power play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wheras I think at the low level, the play-acted power will do.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T11:15:13-07:00","id":584911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=584869#post584869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wheras I think at the low level, the play-acted power will do.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, would you also let a Tyrant satisfy their hunger (at low levels, of course) by playing the power mad villain in a movie? How about in an RPG? Winning a game of Risk? Would you let a Predator satisfy their hunger by playing paintball? How about Call of Duty? Or hide-and-seek?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T11:59:52-07:00","id":584976,"title":"","content":"I think people are mistaking what I'm saying for &quot;You can't do BDSM to satisfy your Hunger&quot; which isn't what I necessarily mean. I mean, you could set out to do that, but when you ACTUALLY satisfy your Hunger, it's when you've sort of moved beyond the point of safety words, you know, the point where the other person isn't just pretending to be powerless (which is what is going on in <i>real </i>BDSM), they <i>actually are</i> (this is bad), which is where all of this gets messy and ugly, it's why I'd be careful around a Hunger like this.<br /> <br /> Like, I could imagine a Predator satisfying his hunger by playing Paintball, but it's not satisfied until he's scared the <i>shit </i>out of somebody in the game. Like, even if it's only for a moment, made them genuinely fear for their life. Think in the movie when the total psychopath is standing over the main character in a seemingly innocuous situation, but to that character it's <i>intensely </i>scary because they fear for their life in imagining what this person could do to them in different circumstances.<br /> <br /> Or in the case of playing Call of Duty as a Tyrant, that's only satisfying your Hunger when you've beaten your friend and gloated and demeaned her to the point where you've seriously upset her. Because just joshing around isn't an actual display of dominance, the Horror isn't satisfied by milquetoast fake bullshit. It's gotta be the real deal.<br /> <br /> I could see an actor playing a villain, but it's gotta be that fella that gets SO into character that he actually scares/upsets the protagonist. Think the dark said of Daniel Day Lewis method acting on the set of <i>Gangs of New York</i>.<br /> <br /> All of this sounds terrible, possibly petulant and definitely abusive, which I'm not sure if that's still the point, but like Satchel said, the removal of the <i>really </i>petty light stuff is definitely suggestive of the idea that no minor fake shit will do.<br /> <br /> But, maybe I'm getting it wrong now that lessons are involved. I still think the Hungers are pretty nasty, but possibly they're not as nasty as I'm suggesting here, but I'm not sure I'll have an idea of how far is too far until the actual real deal final text is out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-09-2015, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:01:28-07:00","id":584979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=584911#post584911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, would you also let a Tyrant satisfy their hunger (at low levels, of course) by playing the power mad villain in a movie? How about in an RPG? Winning a game of Risk? Would you let a Predator satisfy their hunger by playing paintball? How about Call of Duty? Or hide-and-seek?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably only at really low levels of Satiety. And they'd have to <i>crush</i> the other players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:30:04-07:00","id":585028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=584976#post584976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see an actor playing a villain, but it's gotta be that fella that gets SO into character that he actually scares/upsets the protagonist. Think the dark said of Daniel Day Lewis method acting on the set of <i>Gangs of New York</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you would actually need to upset anyone for it to work. I mean in a hypothetical you could also pull it off by just being the better actor to such an extent that the other actor(s) are left sort of dumbfounded about how they're suppose to match you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:33:16-07:00","id":585031,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but I don't imagine that happens passively. You've got to be really good and really critical. The kind of person people are desperate to please and terrified of disappointing, and you let them know they disappointed you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:42:15-07:00","id":585037,"title":"","content":"I'm not really sold either way on this yet, but I'm finding a lot of the comments about BDSM... kind of condescending missing the point of BDSM.<br /> <br /> BDSM is consensual, and as safe as the people involved make it, but it isn't fake. It isn't acting or pretending. If one could distill BDSM to a single &quot;point,&quot; it would be to create genuine emotions/sensations through controlled activities. In &quot;real&quot; BDSM, if the sub wants to feel powerless, the goal of the dominant is to make them feel powerless. Safewords are just a safety measure because that's not an inherently simple or safe (either physically or emotionally) activity. They might not actually be powerless, but they want to feel that way.<br /> <br /> To me, comparing BDSM to acting is like saying that getting punched in boxing isn't &quot;really&quot; getting punched because it's a controlled sport, not a back-alley brawl that is going to end in someone going to the hospital.<br /> <br /> Why I'm still waffling a bit, is I think for something like the Hunger for Power, there's a question of what's more important: the reality of the situation, or the reality of the emotions of people involved.<br /> <br /> Does it matter that the other person genuinely felt powerless even if they weren't, or if you make the target powerless whether they really emotionally feel a complete lack of control?<br /> <br /> A lot of the arguments for seem to be assuming that the feeling of the Tyrant's subject is most important, while a lot of the arguments against seem to be more rooted in the total reality of the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:51:59-07:00","id":585045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585037#post585037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sold either way on this yet, but I'm finding a lot of the comments about BDSM... kind of condescending missing the point of BDSM.<br /> <br /> BDSM is consensual, and as safe as the people involved make it, but it isn't fake. It isn't acting or pretending. If one could distill BDSM to a single &amp;quot;point,&amp;quot; it would be to create genuine emotions/sensations through controlled activities. In &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; BDSM, if the sub wants to feel powerless, the goal of the dominant is to make them feel powerless. Safewords are just a safety measure because that's not an inherently simple or safe (either physically or emotionally) activity. They might not actually be powerless, but they want to feel that way.<br /> <br /> To me, comparing BDSM to acting is like saying that getting punched in boxing isn't &amp;quot;really&amp;quot; getting punched because it's a controlled sport, not a back-alley brawl that is going to end in someone going to the hospital.<br /> <br /> Why I'm still waffling a bit, is I think for something like the Hunger for Power, there's a question of what's more important: the reality of the situation, or the reality of the emotions of people involved.<br /> <br /> Does it matter that the other person genuinely felt powerless even if they weren't, or if you make the target powerless whether they really emotionally feel a complete lack of control?<br /> <br /> A lot of the arguments for seem to be assuming that the feeling of the Tyrant's subject is most important, while a lot of the arguments against seem to be more rooted in the total reality of the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Ok, that's a good distinction to make. If the prey's perception is more important than the reality of the situation, then I could potentially see a power play scene satisfying a hunger for power, or a punishment scene satisfying a hunger for punishment. I'm still iffy on that though, because in order to avoid abusive territory, the sub(s) need(s) to know that they're actually safe. That the moment they decide they don't want to feel powerless any more, the scene will end. I also just find it really difficult to picture a Tyrant using BDSM to feed and then following through with after care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T13:10:20-07:00","id":585061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=584979#post584979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably only at really low levels of Satiety. And they'd have to <i>crush</i> the other players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, see, if you do this, you've effectively transformed &quot;Eldritch Horror&quot; into &quot;Angry Video Game Nerd&quot;<br /> Suddenly, the sanity blasting monstrocity from outside time and space has been transformed into the angry preteen who yells at people over Team Speak.<br /> Next you're going to suggest letting him feed by writing nasty words to people over Twitter...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:30:51-07:00","id":585203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585037#post585037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sold either way on this yet, but I'm finding a lot of the comments about BDSM... kind of condescending missing the point of BDSM.<br /> <br /> BDSM is consensual, and as safe as the people involved make it, but it isn't fake. It isn't acting or pretending. If one could distill BDSM to a single &quot;point,&quot; it would be to create genuine emotions/sensations through controlled activities. In &quot;real&quot; BDSM, if the sub wants to feel powerless, the goal of the dominant is to make them feel powerless. Safewords are just a safety measure because that's not an inherently simple or safe (either physically or emotionally) activity. They might not actually be powerless, but they want to feel that way.<br /> <br /> *snip*<br /> <br /> Why I'm still waffling a bit, is I think for something like the Hunger for Power, there's a question of what's more important: the reality of the situation, or the reality of the emotions of people involved.<br /> <br /> Does it matter that the other person genuinely felt powerless even if they weren't, or if you make the target powerless whether they really emotionally feel a complete lack of control?<br /> <br /> A lot of the arguments for seem to be assuming that the feeling of the Tyrant's subject is most important, while a lot of the arguments against seem to be more rooted in the total reality of the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so speaking as someone with a fair bit of personal experience in the matter: the question isn't whether the emotional aspect of a scene is real. You can make a sub scream, or cry, or shudder in terror that is totally genuine in the moment, but unless you're totally tone deaf or a complete waste of a human being it isn't meant to last. The thing that I've been getting at, and that I think most of the others are, is that it hinges on consent. Even if they feel powerless, the sub knows they aren't at some level, and the Tyrant knows they aren't. The sub hasn't been forced into the position of weakness, they are there by choice, and that is counter to the core idea of the Hunger for Power.<br /> <br /> They aren't sated by someone kneeling before them, but by crushing the will of their meal until it's knees buckle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T16:18:18-07:00","id":585325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585045#post585045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still iffy on that though, because in order to avoid abusive territory, the sub(s) need(s) to know that they're actually safe. That the moment they decide they don't want to feel powerless any more, the scene will end. I also just find it really difficult to picture a Tyrant using BDSM to feed and then following through with after care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I'm not really decided on where I fall on this.<br /> <br /> Though rereading the revised Tyrant right up, the Hunger for Power is described as the Tyrant feeling superior, and offers the lessons of pushing people to their limits.<br /> <br /> As such, the ability for a sub to red doesn't seem entirely relevant. A Tyrant besting an co-worker for a promotion and reveling in it works. It doesn't matter that the co-worker could have beaten them out for it. The Tyrant only needs the feeling of superiority.<br /> <br /> Heck, I know sadists that negotiate scenes for the express purpose of getting their partner to call red. If they're in that head space, they demonstrate they're superior abilities to inflict pain by pushing their partner to the limit; that no matter how long their partner tries to hold out they'll cave and call red because they can't take it any longer.<br /> <br /> On the point about aftercare, I can see that, though I know people that do not use dominant play partners for aftercare and have designated third parties to handle that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585203#post585203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the question isn't whether the emotional aspect of a scene is real. You can make a sub scream, or cry, or shudder in terror that is totally genuine in the moment,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, but I wasn't just responding to you. Honestly the particular part about the real emotions derived from BDSM play was much more inspired by Charlaquin's previous comments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They aren't sated by someone kneeling before them, but by crushing the will of their meal until it's knees buckle. </div> </div> </div>I'm not really convinced the Tyrant section really supports this distinction. Both seem viable options (even if the first might not work forever) according to the text.<br /> <br /> &quot;They bask in the fear, respect, and trembling worship of those beneath them, whether the Beast is standing at the top of the pyramid or controlling things from the shadows while their subjects tremble at the thought of their unseen king.&quot;<br /> <br /> That doesn't really seem to necessitate a lack of consent. Willing submission might not by itself sate the Hunger, but exercising the control willing submission allows seems like it would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T16:28:41-07:00","id":585337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585325#post585325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not really convinced the Tyrant section really supports this distinction. Both seem viable options (even if the first might not work forever) according to the text.<br /> <br /> &quot;They bask in the fear, respect, and trembling worship of those beneath them, whether the Beast is standing at the top of the pyramid or controlling things from the shadows while their subjects tremble at the thought of their unseen king.&quot;<br /> <br /> That doesn't really seem to necessitate a lack of consent. Willing submission might not by itself sate the Hunger, but exercising the control willing submission allows seems like it would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably depends on how hard said submission would be to acquire. I mean lets be fair there is a difference between someone who wants to serve submit and the like vs forcing a bunch of people who are convinced they are the best at something to accept that you are superior to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:14:49-07:00","id":585395,"title":"","content":"The difference comes from the &quot;shock&quot; that's a huge thing in the new draft. You need a lesson or moment of realization. For someone that willingly and knowingly submits, there's nothing to feed on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T18:22:38-07:00","id":585505,"title":"","content":"I know a lot of people in the BDSM community that would disagree with the idea that there's no moment of lesson/realization. They can find out they can be pushed farther physically, emotionally, or psychologically then they thought they could. Things they thought were limits can be softened, explored, and surpassed.<br /> <br /> Willing submission doesn't mean you don't have limits on what you're willing to do (that's why healthy BDSM stresses consent so strongly), and pushing limits is explicitly something the Tyrant write-up states is part of their thing regarding lessons. If my Tyrant Dom beats a partner to red (on purpose as negotiated), there's a significant chance it pushes them to expand their limits in some fashion thanks to my character's superior sadism. How is that not something to feed on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T19:20:13-07:00","id":585525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585395#post585395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference comes from the &quot;shock&quot; that's a huge thing in the new draft. You need a lesson or moment of realization. For someone that willingly and knowingly submits, there's nothing to feed on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree since that would imply feeding necessitates a lesson and its kind of an established fact that your Horror doesn't care about lessons, so long as food is involved.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T20:37:30-07:00","id":585583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585525#post585525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would disagree since that would imply feeding necessitates a lesson and its kind of an established fact that your Horror doesn't care about lessons, so long as food is involved.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its not necessarily a lesson, but the revised chapters are pretty clear on there being a need for a shock or realization of some kind. Its not enough for a collector to get some shiny gemstones - someone has to actually feel the loss for it to count, for example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T20:48:40-07:00","id":585585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585505#post585505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my Tyrant Dom beats a partner to red (on purpose as negotiated), there's a significant chance it pushes them to expand their limits in some fashion thanks to my character's superior sadism. How is that not something to feed on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did the partner consent to having their limits pushed? Then that steals some of the authority from the Tyrant and probably denies them a meal. Did the partner not consent to having their limits pushed, and the Tyrant went too far to get her meal? That's abuse and she gets her meal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 07-09-2015, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:21:08-07:00","id":585624,"title":"","content":"I think I'm going to have to side with Heavy Arms on this one. The Tyrant write up does seem to be about pushing boundaries more than outright violating them. Even if said boundary pushing is completely consensual and agreed upon, it's definitely still a pushing of boundaries. A big thing for a lot of subs is seeing just how far they can go before they absolutely <i>have</i> to tap out. That might very well mean denying yourself the ability to exercise your power, even when you are actually terrified of being powerless, just to prove to yourself that you can do it. As long as this is all pre-negotiated and consensual, and you retain the ability to safe word out if and when you need to... Yeah, I could see that satisfying the Dom's hunger for power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T23:28:18-07:00","id":585711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585585#post585585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the partner consent to having their limits pushed? Then that steals some of the authority from the Tyrant and probably denies them a meal. Did the partner not consent to having their limits pushed, and the Tyrant went too far to get her meal? That's abuse and she gets her meal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is it stated in the text that this distinction matters?<br /> <br /> Tyrants feed off of things that flaunt their superiority and push the limits of those beneath them.<br /> <br /> I find the whole argument that Tyrants can't have willing subordinates and sate themselves by flaunting their power over them, essentially cuts off any sort of social or mental based Tyrant. The text has an example of a Tyrant feeding from being a competitor for a promotion, and then using their new found power to embarrass their former rival. By the logic being used above, since the rival could quit the job and avoid being made to polish the Tyrant's new name plate, it steals some of the authority from the Tyrant and denies them the meal.<br /> <br /> Maybe this stems from my personal philosophic views on the nature of social power, but as I see it (and I feel the text follows this) social power is inherently an emergent property of a group's social contract/norms. The societies we create, create the disparities that lead to some people having more social power than others. These rules though, can be changed, and thus change who has power and who doesn't. That change is not solely in the hands of those with power. Basically, if Tyrants can only feed by denying others completely of agency (something I don't see in the text), they can't feed in social situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T04:50:15-07:00","id":585872,"title":"","content":"It does come up with a question, doesn't it? What happens with those the Tyrant has already gotten to submit? Does he grow tired of them and move on to new challenges? Only keep them around in hope of a rebellion? Is it possible to have continuous relationships? <br /> <br /> Does having subordinates actually matter to a Tyrant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T05:49:53-07:00","id":585933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585872#post585872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does come up with a question, doesn't it? What happens with those the Tyrant has already gotten to submit? Does he grow tired of them and move on to new challenges? Only keep them around in hope of a rebellion? Is it possible to have continuous relationships? <br /> <br /> Does having subordinates actually matter to a Tyrant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say yes their is long term relationship for tyrants in the case of subordinates. An example for tyrants is becoming head of one big international company that would imply that anyone who is below his rank in the company would be considered a subordinate and you do not fire your employees just because you grow tired of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T06:14:38-07:00","id":585974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=584911#post584911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, would you also let a Tyrant satisfy their hunger (at low levels, of course) by playing the power mad villain in a movie? How about in an RPG? Winning a game of Risk? Would you let a Predator satisfy their hunger by playing paintball? How about Call of Duty? Or hide-and-seek?</div> </div> </div> </div>In order... No, no, if it was with strangers, yes, no, and maybe.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T06:24:46-07:00","id":585983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585974#post585974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order... No, no, if it was with strangers, yes, no, and maybe.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely don't see where you're drawing the line between pretend dominance and actual dominance. Could you explain your criteria? What is it about winning Risk with strangers that makes it a genuine source of power when playing a corrupt warlord in a movie is not? What makes Paintball a legitimate source of predation when Call of Duty is not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T07:02:26-07:00","id":586052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585983#post585983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely don't see where you're drawing the line between pretend dominance and actual dominance. Could you explain your criteria? What is it about winning Risk with strangers that makes it a genuine source of power when playing a corrupt warlord in a movie is not? What makes Paintball a legitimate source of predation when Call of Duty is not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing Risk involves an actual competition you can win, and make other people lose - more so if it's strangers - whereas a movie doesn't even have the illusion of <i>you</i> having power over anyone. Paintball involves the physical stalking of people (multiplayer Call of Duty is at too much of a remove to count as Prey for me, though I might allow it for Power under the competition aspect).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:09:37-07:00","id":586279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585711#post585711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is it stated in the text that this distinction matters?</div> </div> </div> </div>The overall themes of the book. Hunger is one of the most important driving elements of the book. Having a bunch of completely willing people let you dominate them / steal from them / hunt them should never be a long term solution to your hunger. Of course, there does exist room for allowing that kind of thing if the storyteller does not want Hunger to play a central theme in his Beast game, or allows the scenario as a temporary island of calm between storms. But otherwise? That would be too easy. Beasts do not even get a Feeding Grounds merit the way Vampires do.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=585711#post585711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the whole argument that Tyrants can't have willing subordinates and sate themselves by flaunting their power over them, essentially cuts off any sort of social or mental based Tyrant. The text has an example of a Tyrant feeding from being a competitor for a promotion, and then using their new found power to embarrass their former rival. By the logic being used above, since the rival could quit the job and avoid being made to polish the Tyrant's new name plate, it steals some of the authority from the Tyrant and denies them the meal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should depend on whether or not genuine abuse is happening. Every single one of the Hungers requires some kind of loss or trauma from the victim. You absolutely can have a circle of willing people and feed from them as long as you are pushing them too far, demanding too much, and the whole thing is eventually going to break. Even if you genuinely don't want to hurt them. The consent portion itself is not the issue -- plenty of people are going to consent to a mind blowingly attractive Makara. It's the safe part of the equation that should make it stop counting as a meal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 07-10-2015, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:24:10-07:00","id":586289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586052#post586052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing Risk involves an actual competition you can win, and make other people lose - more so if it's strangers - whereas a movie doesn't even have the illusion of <i>you</i> having power over anyone. Paintball involves the physical stalking of people (multiplayer Call of Duty is at too much of a remove to count as Prey for me, though I might allow it for Power under the competition aspect).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See, I'd be more inclined to put BDSM on the level of acting. In both cases, you're creating a genuine emotional reaction in response to an artificial or manufactured scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:07:50-07:00","id":586313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586289#post586289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I'd be more inclined to put BDSM on the level of acting. In both cases, you're creating a genuine emotional reaction in response to an artificial or manufactured scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div> Here's the problem, though. In BDSM, you're evoking real emotional reactions in someone. In a movie? You're not. Or, rather, you're evoking the wrong kind of emotions. On the set, you're not going to be scaring a fellow actor or actress into submission through your part. None of the crew will be. And, once it hits the theaters, sure, there'll be emotional reactions from the audience, but it won't be them feeling the Tyrant as being superior.<br /> <br /> Part of feeding the Hunger seems to be that these need to be <i>personal</i>. A third party audience will be too removed. A fellow actress or actor is your partner in this endeavor, not your target, so they won't be evoking the right emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-10-2015, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:33:18-07:00","id":586335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586279#post586279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The overall themes of the book. Hunger is one of the most important driving elements of the book. Having a bunch of completely willing people let you dominate them / steal from them / hunt them should never be a long term solution to your hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except its not. Even with allowing it, such feeding of your Hunger only pass for Low Satiety. Anything more requires far more effort to hunt down to feed on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But otherwise? That would be too easy. </div> </div> </div> Low Satiety feeding is easy, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts do not even get a Feeding Grounds merit the way Vampires do. </div> </div> </div> No, Beasts don't get a feeding ground merit like vamps, nor a locus like wolves, hallow like mages, glamour from fruit, pledges, emotion, or dreams like changelings, haunts like sin-eaters, infrastructure like demons, or geomantic tombs like mummies. Prommies don't have feeding grounds either, but for a different reason.<br /> <br /> However! Beasts do get Family Dinner, which can actually function pretty close to a vampire's Herd. Simply hanging out with a vamp as he has breakfast is enough for a free point of Satiety. An Iron Master on the police could give a Beast free Satiety when they chase down criminals - that's a valid hunt by the new WtF book. Emotion feeding Summer changelings could go to sport game together for a free hit on both sides.<br /> <br /> The truth is that, sometimes, feeding is actually pretty easy. Keeping it at medium or high satiety is difficult, but if its just low Satiety? Its easy to run off your Hunger alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It should depend on whether or not genuine abuse is happening. Every single one of the Hungers requires some kind of loss or trauma from the victim. </div> </div> </div> No, no it doesn't. A Tyrant can get Satiety from winning a boxing match. That's neither abuse nor trauma. Abuse is not required.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's the safe part of the equation that should make it stop counting as a meal. </div> </div> </div> Collectors can get Satiety without endangering lives by swiping items that will be missed; could even feed by being a narcotics cop, getting drugs off the street. Why should Tyrant be different?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:37:20-07:00","id":586356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586313#post586313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here's the problem, though. In BDSM, you're evoking real emotional reactions in someone. In a movie? You're not. Or, rather, you're evoking the wrong kind of emotions. On the set, you're not going to be scaring a fellow actor or actress into submission through your part. None of the crew will be. And, once it hits the theaters, sure, there'll be emotional reactions from the audience, but it won't be them feeling the Tyrant as being superior.<br /> <br /> Part of feeding the Hunger seems to be that these need to be <i>personal</i>. A third party audience will be too removed. A fellow actress or actor is your partner in this endeavor, not your target, so they won't be evoking the right emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, I can see some Directors being Beasts.<br /> Some of them have done some really shady or dangerous shit to get a real emotional reaction out of actors.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:41:26-07:00","id":586358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586313#post586313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here's the problem, though. In BDSM, you're evoking real emotional reactions in someone. In a movie? You're not. Or, rather, you're evoking the wrong kind of emotions. On the set, you're not going to be scaring a fellow actor or actress into submission through your part.</div> </div> </div> </div>You will if your fellow actor is worth their salt at the craft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:57:08-07:00","id":586371,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... perhaps. I don't quite think of it that way, but I can see your point of view. For me, there's two criteria for feeding Satiety through your Hunger.<br /> <br /> One, it has to be a shock, an emotional thrill, of some kind. As long as the emotion happens, and its real, it counts. <br /> Two, it needs to feed into and grow the Legend somehow. This is more of a flavor thing- some collectors want gold and art, some want lovers, etc. Role playing and acting both count, since we're talking about the astral-dream reflections here. <br /> <br /> So long as the emotion evoked is real and of appropriate flavor, I would say that it counts. I don't particularly see how safety, consent, or the like fit in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T13:05:10-07:00","id":586400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586371#post586371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... perhaps. I don't quite think of it that way, but I can see your point of view. For me, there's two criteria for feeding Satiety through your Hunger.<br /> <br /> One, it has to be a shock, an emotional thrill, of some kind. As long as the emotion happens, and its real, it counts. <br /> Two, it needs to feed into and grow the Legend somehow. This is more of a flavor thing- some collectors want gold and art, some want lovers, etc. Role playing and acting both count, since we're talking about the astral-dream reflections here. <br /> <br /> So long as the emotion evoked is real and of appropriate flavor, I would say that it counts. I don't particularly see how safety, consent, or the like fit in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, in the case of acting, I suppose it does depend very much on the actors and techniques they use. &quot;Method acting&quot; and other techniques derived from it like the Meisner technique are <i>all about</i> having very real emotional responses. I figure if you've dedicated years of study and rehearsal to such a technique, that should be real enough to count for Satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T13:07:18-07:00","id":586402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586289#post586289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I'd be more inclined to put BDSM on the level of acting. In both cases, you're creating a genuine emotional reaction in response to an artificial or manufactured scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'm going back to the boxing comparison:<br /> <br /> You're basically saying that two guys wailing on each other for 30 minutes trying to actually hurt each other, but in a controlled environment for entertainment, is no different that fight choreography in an action movie where most &quot;hits&quot; don't even connect where the point is to fake a fight.<br /> <br /> Acting is about convincing the audience that your character is experiencing something so they have a genuine emotional reaction to it. BDSM is about about experiencing something so you have a genuine emotional reaction to it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T13:16:11-07:00","id":586411,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm not really that familiar with acting techniques, so I'll take your word for it. Feeding Hungers are a very individualized thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T13:25:18-07:00","id":586413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586402#post586402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acting is about convincing the audience that your character is experiencing something so they have a genuine emotional reaction to it. BDSM is about about experiencing something so you have a genuine emotional reaction to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, (good) acting is about actually experiencing genuine emotional reactions to the artificial situations your character is in, thereby allowing the audience the catharsis of witnessing those genuine emotions. When a (good) actor cries onstage or in a film, they are actually feeling that. No amount of fancy camera tricks can substitute for real human emotion. Literally, we spend years and a lot of money learning to access real, actual emotions at any time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T13:59:53-07:00","id":586429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586402#post586402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I'm going back to the boxing comparison:</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think boxing is a valid comparison. When two people are boxing, they both genuinely want to win. One of them eventually does win and the other person experiences a genuine sense of loss. A Beast boxer could definitely feed off another boxer.<br /> <br /> Your comparison is closer to the WWF, where both participants put on a show and may have genuinely strong emotions during the performance, but the end result is almost always scripted. A Beast wrestler probably cannot feed off another wrestler unless he took it too far and became abusive during the match.<br /> <br /> Now, the wrestling manager who gets to tell some of the wrestlers under him that they have to take a fall? That could definitely be a Beast.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T17:58:04-07:00","id":586649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586413#post586413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, (good) acting is about actually experiencing genuine emotional reactions to the artificial situations your character is in, thereby allowing the audience the catharsis of witnessing those genuine emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels far too much like treating specific schools of acting as the One True Way of acting.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, outside of the philosophies of different schools of acting, it doesn't matter if the actor is actually experiencing genuine emotional audiences as long as the audience buys into the performance. <br /> <br /> I'm completely on board with the idea that experiencing genuine emotional reactions is the most effective process for an actor to accomplish the goal of acting. But saying it is the only way to good acting strikes me as something that can be fairly easily shown to not be the case. I consider William H. Macy a good actor, and he isn't a method actor. He practices an acting technique that focuses on using your personal experiences to replace the character's experiences, rather than trying to experience what the character experiences.<br /> <br /> You're also still avoiding the very troublesome nature of asserting that BDSM is an act. Even if &quot;acting&quot; has a far less negative connotation for you than it does in general use, it still means the point of what you're doing is for the benefit of the audience, not yourself. BDSM isn't for an audience's catharsis. It's for the participants catharsis. I don't think this is a difference that can just be tossed aside.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586429#post586429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think boxing is a valid comparison. When two people are boxing, they both genuinely want to win. One of them eventually does win and the other person experiences a genuine sense of loss. A Beast boxer could definitely feed off another boxer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the point of the boxing comparison. The points of the boxing comparison are that being in a controlled environment doesn't detract from the potential for feeding, and that there's a difference between two people engaged in an actual activity, and two people faking being in that activity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your comparison is closer to the WWF, where both participants put on a show and may have genuinely strong emotions during the performance, but the end result is almost always scripted. </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much the exact opposite of my point, so I don't see how that's closer to my comparison.<br /> <br /> BDSM isn't about putting on a show, and isn't inherently about following a script.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T18:21:00-07:00","id":586663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586649#post586649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This feels far too much like treating specific schools of acting as the One True Way of acting.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, outside of the philosophies of different schools of acting, it doesn't matter if the actor is actually experiencing genuine emotional audiences as long as the audience buys into the performance. <br /> <br /> I'm completely on board with the idea that experiencing genuine emotional reactions is the most effective process for an actor to accomplish the goal of acting. But saying it is the only way to good acting strikes me as something that can be fairly easily shown to not be the case. I consider William H. Macy a good actor, and he isn't a method actor. He practices an acting technique that focuses on using your personal experiences to replace the character's experiences, rather than trying to experience what the character experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's called the Meisner technique, it's derived from &quot;the Method&quot; and it's also the technique I was trained in. It's still about having a genuine emotional response, it's just more about achieving that response through recalling your own past experiences rather than recreating the experiences your character is having. As one of my best acting teachers put it, if you're playing the role of a prostitute, Stanislovsky would have said, &quot;you'd better go turn a trick if you want to portray this role effectively&quot; whereas Meisner would have said, &quot;think of a time when you felt like a whore, and use that.&quot; But you're right, that was unfair of me to suggest it's the only way to act well. That said, most of the best actors today do use some technique to elicit genuine emotions within themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586649#post586649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're also still avoiding the very troublesome nature of asserting that BDSM is an act. Even if &quot;acting&quot; has a far less negative connotation for you than it does in general use, it still means the point of what you're doing is for the benefit of the audience, not yourself. BDSM isn't for an audience's catharsis. It's for the participants catharsis. I don't think this is a difference that can just be tossed aside.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I'm trying to suggest at all. I'm saying that neither BDSM nor acting is &quot;an act.&quot; In both cases, the goal is to evoke actual emotions in yourself, your partner(s), and any audience you may have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-10-2015, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T19:54:07-07:00","id":586717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586663#post586663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's called the Meisner technique, it's derived from &quot;the Method&quot; and it's also the technique I was trained in. It's still about having a genuine emotional response, it's just more about achieving that response through recalling your own past experiences rather than recreating the experiences your character is having. As one of my best acting teachers put it, if you're playing the role of a prostitute, Stanislovsky would have said, &quot;you'd better go turn a trick if you want to portray this role effectively&quot; whereas Meisner would have said, &quot;think of a time when you felt like a whore, and use that.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Here's the thing, though. Using one of them - experiencing the emotion directly by putting yourself in the character's position - is valid. Channeling your emotion from another point in time - specifically a point in time that had nothing to do with our Tyrant - would not be. A Tyrant has to be the subject of the actor's submission, not someone or something else else.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T20:35:01-07:00","id":586738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586717#post586717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here's the thing, though. Using one of them - experiencing the emotion directly by putting yourself in the character's position - is valid. Channeling your emotion from another point in time - specifically a point in time that had nothing to do with our Tyrant - would not be. A Tyrant has to be the subject of the actor's submission, not someone or something else else.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what criteria are we working from here? Evidently it's not the genuineness of the emotion, it's the source?<br /> <br /> Also, does the Tyrant feed on the victim's feelings of powerlessness, or their own feeling of power over others?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T23:56:07-07:00","id":586861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586649#post586649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not the point of the boxing comparison. The points of the boxing comparison are that being in a controlled environment doesn't detract from the potential for feeding, and that there's a difference between two people engaged in an actual activity, and two people faking being in that activity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree that being in a controlled environment doesn't detract from the potential for feeding. But that is not why the Boxing comparison fails. The boxing ring would be a valid feeding ground because the domination and defeat is <i>really happening</i>. There is a genuine sense of loss that comes from it. The opponent <i>sincerely wanted to win. </i>The fact that it is a controlled environment is neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, only an unhealthy BDSM relationship is going to have the loss, misery, and sadness that fills the belly of a Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 07-11-2015, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T05:14:56-07:00","id":586989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586738#post586738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what criteria are we working from here? Evidently it's not the genuineness of the emotion, it's the source?<br /> <br /> Also, does the Tyrant feed on the victim's feelings of powerlessness, or their own feeling of power over others?</div> </div> </div> </div> according to revised chapter, you need a spark that relates to growing the Legend of your Horror. So, the Tyrant gains Satiety from someone submitting to her personally. Still needs to be a genuine emotion, but not so much the source as... Direction, i'd say is a good term. The emotion needs to be directed at the Tyrant. Evoking the emotion of a previous event isn't directed at the beast in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T05:18:16-07:00","id":586990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586861#post586861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely agree that being in a controlled environment doesn't detract from the potential for feeding. But that is not why the Boxing comparison fails. The boxing ring would be a valid feeding ground because the domination and defeat is <i>really happening</i>. There is a genuine sense of loss that comes from it. The opponent <i>sincerely wanted to win. </i>The fact that it is a controlled environment is neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, only an unhealthy BDSM relationship is going to have the loss, misery, and sadness that fills the belly of a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div> i find the implication that healthy BDSM doesn't have real emotion to be insulting. Furthermore, Hunger is not about loss, misery, and sadness, its about a teaching lessons. You have a misunderstanding of what Hunger is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T08:30:19-07:00","id":587143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586990#post586990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> i find the implication that healthy BDSM doesn't have real emotion to be insulting. Furthermore, Hunger is not about loss, misery, and sadness, its about a teaching lessons. You have a misunderstanding of what Hunger is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats not really what he said though.<br /> What he said is merely that the terror and powerlessness isn't real. Since those particular feelings aren't real, the Beast cant feed off of false emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T10:09:15-07:00","id":587228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586663#post586663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's called the Meisner technique, it's derived from &quot;the Method&quot; and it's also the technique I was trained in.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC William H. Macy uses Practical Aesthetics, not the Meisner technique (though as I understand it, it draws heavily on both Meisner and Stanislavsky).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not what I'm trying to suggest at all. I'm saying that neither BDSM nor acting is &quot;an act.&quot; In both cases, the goal is to evoke actual emotions in yourself, your partner(s), and any audience you may have. </div> </div> </div>I appreciate that, but before I popped into the thread, there was a bit more talk of BDSM as being an act. You didn't use the word fakery, but you're response to Leetspeek seemed to be in support of that assessment. So it feels like you were going along with BDSM as an &quot;act,&quot; and then furthering it by continually defending it in comparison to acting.<br /> <br /> For those of us that aren't trained actors, it's really hard to separate someone calling something &quot;acting,&quot; but not &quot;an act.&quot; as different things. I hope this explains my reactions a bit more thoroughly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=586861#post586861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely agree that being in a controlled environment doesn't detract from the potential for feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't really mesh with some of your previous posts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that is not why the Boxing comparison fails. </div> </div> </div>Then it doesn't fail. Because that's all it's trying to say on that regard. Comparisons and analogies aren't perfect rhetorical devices. I'm don't care about it failing in regards to things I'm not using it for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile, only an unhealthy BDSM relationship is going to have the loss, misery, and sadness that fills the belly of a Beast. </div> </div> </div>Beasts don't all feed on loss, misery, and sadness. We have different Hungers for a reason. Some Hungers can be sated by certain activities, and others can't. You might as well be saying that any activity that doesn't require the target to roll Integrity doesn't count for feeding. It has as much support in the books as your assertion that all feedings require the same emotions in their targets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587143#post587143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What he said is merely that the terror and powerlessness isn't real. Since those particular feelings aren't real, the Beast cant feed off of false emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except he's not. He's saying the feelings don't matter because they're not what counts.<br /> <br /> And saying they're not real is still incredibly problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T11:04:57-07:00","id":587250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587228#post587228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC William H. Macy uses Practical Aesthetics, not the Meisner technique (though as I understand it, it draws heavily on both Meisner and Stanislavsky).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I appreciate that, but before I popped into the thread, there was a bit more talk of BDSM as being an act. You didn't use the word fakery, but you're response to Leetspeek seemed to be in support of that assessment. So it feels like you were going along with BDSM as an &quot;act,&quot; and then furthering it by continually defending it in comparison to acting.<br /> <br /> For those of us that aren't trained actors, it's really hard to separate someone calling something &quot;acting,&quot; but not &quot;an act.&quot; as different things. I hope this explains my reactions a bit more thoroughly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I gotcha. Yeah, I was originally in the &quot;BDSM wouldn't count for Satiety because it's not actually an unbalanced power dynamic&quot; camp, but you swayed me with your argument that it's more about whether the emotions are real than whether the power dynamic is actually unbalanced. I was extrapolating from that and saying that in my experience with both acting and BDSM, an acting scene creates emotions just as real as those created in a BDSM scene (which is to say, completely real), therefore I believe acting could also be a legitimate source of Satiety, as long as it contributes to the Beast's Legend. Sorry if my stance was unclear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T11:31:37-07:00","id":587273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587143#post587143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats not really what he said though.<br /> What he said is merely that the terror and powerlessness isn't real. Since those particular feelings aren't real, the Beast cant feed off of false emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is frankly the problem. The emotions ARE real, and you don't need <i>loss, misery, and sadness </i>to feed a seductive Tyrant - those were the specific emotions s/he said.<br /> <br /> Between the focus on the wrong emotions, and claiming they're not real? I'm going to say that I flat out disagree with him. There's no real way to misinterpret those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-11-2015, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T12:25:48-07:00","id":587335,"title":"","content":"<b>@Heavy Arms:</b> ...What? I dont know how you interprid the phrase &quot;only an unhealthy BDSM relationship is going to have the loss, misery, and sadness&quot;, but I interprid that as saying &quot;only an unhealthy BDSM relationship is going to have the loss, misery, and sadness&quot;. Or in other words &quot;the terror and powerlessness isn't real&quot;<br /> If you think my liberal interpritation of that phrase is incorrect, please dont hesitate to correct me...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>@MCN:</b> The emotions wouldn't be real in a healthy relationship. Nobody in a healthy relationship is seriously afraid that the other person might kill or mutilate them. Theres no fear, theres no dread. Theres no negative emotions for the Beast to feed upon. Its not that there wont be <i>some</i> real emotions, but they would be more along the lines of &quot;Omg, this is hot as fuck&quot; and less along the lines of &quot;Omg, his going to fucking murder me!&quot;. I dont really find it thematically apropriate to allow the Beast to feed on pretend emotions. As I've said elsewhere, it'de kinda be like allowing a Vampire to regain Vitae by eating a really red steak for dinner.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T13:05:57-07:00","id":587355,"title":"","content":"Krobles, what you're not getting is that in BDSM, the emotions are not fake. Although intellectually you know you're safe, that doesn't make the emotions involved any less real. The whole point is so that someone <i>can</i> experience that fear of &quot;Omg, he's going to fucking kill me&quot;, or the feeling of being powerless, or the feeling of having absolute power over someone else, in a safe space where they aren't actually going to be killed, and all they have to do is say the word and they have their power back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T14:04:25-07:00","id":587408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587228#post587228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't really mesh with some of your previous posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize there are some definition issues happening here. It comes from speaking about broad generalizations and then growing increasingly more specific as the discussion continues. For example, in my first post I was talking about consent in a general way. Then later in another post I narrow it down from consent in a general way to the more specific difference between consenting to be abused versus getting more than you bargained for when you consented.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587228#post587228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it doesn't fail. Because that's all it's trying to say on that regard. Comparisons and analogies aren't perfect rhetorical devices. I'm don't care about it failing in regards to things I'm not using it for.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are not trying to apply the Boxing analogy to BDSM subjugation feeding, then alright. That's fair.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587228#post587228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts don't all feed on loss, misery, and sadness. We have different Hungers for a reason. Some Hungers can be sated by certain activities, and others can't. You might as well be saying that any activity that doesn't require the target to roll Integrity doesn't count for feeding. It has as much support in the books as your assertion that all feedings require the same emotions in their targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of them do, and that is pretty important when speaking about Hungers in general. I accept the existence of certain beasts who may feed specifically on pain, in which case a healthy BDSM relationship might provide that for a little while. But I cannot accept a Tyrant getting food from someone who willingly wants to be subjugated and easily allows themselves to be.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">i find the implication that healthy BDSM doesn't have real emotion to be insulting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The emotions <i>are real</i>, but the subjugation i<i>s not,</i> unless the Dom is abusing the consent of the Sub.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, Hunger is not about loss, misery, and sadness, its about a teaching lessons. You have a misunderstanding of what Hunger is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunger does not care about lessons. The Beast cares about lessons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 07-11-2015, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T14:15:42-07:00","id":587414,"title":"","content":"Firstly, I think saying &quot;Tyrants can&quot; or &quot;Tyrants can't&quot; is sort of missing the mark. Two Beasts with a Hunger for Power don't necessarily feel it in the same way, so there probably are some for whom consensual BDSM is a viable way to feed and for others it isn't.<br /> <br /> Secondly, on the subject of emotions, have you never been genuinely sad because a character in a movie, book, or game you were invested in died? Have you never been scared by an amusement park ride? Human entertainment is pretty much just finding different ways to evoke emotional responses, I don't think that makes them any less real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T15:02:44-07:00","id":587450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The emotions <i>are real</i>, but the subjugation i<i>s not,</i> unless the Dom is abusing the consent of the Sub. </div> </div> </div> This statement that you cannot have sexual submission outside of an abusive relationship is just plain ignorant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T15:42:13-07:00","id":587468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587355#post587355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Krobles, what you're not getting is that in BDSM, the emotions are not fake. Although intellectually you know you're safe, that doesn't make the emotions involved any less real. The whole point is so that someone <i>can</i> experience that fear of &quot;Omg, he's going to fucking kill me&quot;, or the feeling of being powerless, or the feeling of having absolute power over someone else, in a safe space where they aren't actually going to be killed, and all they have to do is say the word and they have their power back.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last part is precisely why I wouldn't consider it valid in the context of the Beast. If the person can have their power back with the utterance of a word, the Beast isn't being the &quot;Tyrant&quot; then.<br /> <br /> Also, in my experience with rough sexual play, I've always known entirely well that the feelings of subjugation I were experiencing were entirely artificial. Goes the other way too, with the feelings of domination being knowingly artificial aswell.<br /> Sure, in the heat of the moment, its not a fact I dwelled upon, but that doesn't mean I wasn't totally and entirely aware of the artificiality of the feelings. Other people might've had different experiences with it then I have had, but in my own personal experience, your statement is incorrect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T15:47:05-07:00","id":587471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587468#post587468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That last part is precisely why I wouldn't consider it valid in the context of the Beast. If the person can have their power back with the utterance of a word, the Beast isn't being the &quot;Tyrant&quot; then.<br /> <br /> Also, in my experience with rough sexual play, I've always known entirely well that the feelings of subjugation I were experiencing were entirely artificial. Goes the other way too, with the feelings of domination being knowingly artificial aswell.<br /> Sure, in the heat of the moment, its not a fact I dwelled upon, but that doesn't mean I wasn't totally and entirely aware of the artificiality of the feelings. Other people might've had different experiences with it then I have had, but in my own personal experience, your statement is incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're certainly aware that the subjugation is artificial, but that doesn't make the feelings artificial. That's the thing about emotions, they're quite often incongruent with our thoughts and/or with reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T16:44:44-07:00","id":587498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587450#post587450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This statement that you cannot have sexual submission outside of an abusive relationship is just plain ignorant.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're free to disagree with the opinion, but there is nothing ignorant about it. Either your partner has consented and agreed to explore the limits of sexual submission that they can handle (in which case the meal is hollow), you forced the agreement (abusive relationship), or you are ignoring the level of sexual submission that has been asked of you (abusive relationship).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T17:31:59-07:00","id":587566,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm going to reassert a previous challenge:<br /> <br /> Cite the revised preview texts. You keep asserting things about both Hunger and Tyrants, but I really am not seeing this in the text as it stands.<br /> <br /> It isn't even a consistent position. You agree you can feed off of beating someone in a boxing match, but your opponent consented to being there, consented to a set of rules that dictate who the winner is, and so on. But the consent there doesn't matter. The artificial constraints don't matter. You can win and feed.<br /> <br /> But in BDSM, consent and external rules suddenly make the meal inherently hollow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T18:13:13-07:00","id":587578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587468#post587468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That last part is precisely why I wouldn't consider it valid in the context of the Beast. If the person can have their power back with the utterance of a word, the Beast isn't being the &quot;Tyrant&quot; then.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can always take power back from a Tyrant in a social situation by choosing to not play his game. Or, in a physical situation, I could take power back by pointing a gun at him. At the furthest extreme, I can regain power by exercising, getting physically strong, trained in fighting, and beating him down.<br /> <br /> There's always the potential to take power back at any point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, in my experience with rough sexual play, I've always known entirely well that the feelings of subjugation I were experiencing were entirely artificial. Goes the other way too, with the feelings of domination being knowingly artificial as well.<br /> <br /> Sure, in the heat of the moment, its not a fact I dwelled upon, but that doesn't mean I wasn't totally and entirely aware of the artificiality of the feelings. Other people might've had different experiences with it then I have had, but in my own personal experience, your statement is incorrect. </div> </div> </div> So you would make shitty target for Hunger. What does that have to do with finding the people who would? Not everyone is ticklish either. Needs Must is prefect for finding the people that are willing to submit. And all we need is one person to prove it true.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587498#post587498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're free to disagree with the opinion, but there is nothing ignorant about it. Either your partner has consented and agreed to explore the limits of sexual submission that they can handle<u><b> (in which case the meal is hollow), </b></u>you forced the agreement (abusive relationship), or you are ignoring the level of sexual submission that has been asked of you (abusive relationship).</div> </div> </div> </div>The selected part is what is ignorant. You are just making up that its hollow. <br /> <br /> What does &quot;its hollow!&quot; even mean, anyways? Penalty to the feeding roll? No one is disputing that. Its easy? All Low Satiety feedings are easy. Not viable? There's no proof that its non-viable. I agree with the above - got quotes to back up your claims?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T18:33:26-07:00","id":587585,"title":"","content":"A Tyrant that's a Dom will basically be setting out to get the Sub to use their safe word. That safe word is going to basically be the queue that he has successfully fed by showing the Sub their limits. The totally depraved people that are down for <b><i>anything</i></b> are not going to be the kind of partner a Tyrant would want. Agreeing to have your limits pushed still involves having your limits pushed. The Tyrant <i>will</i> show them to you and you <i>will</i> back down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T20:44:39-07:00","id":587679,"title":"","content":"Guys, &quot;Someone else is procuring the meal for you: -2 to feeding roll&quot; (page 52 of chapter 3 of revised text). <i>That </i>is how I would handle a regular, 100% consensual and sane BDSM relationship between two willing partners. Just because your prey is the one procuring the meal for you doesn't make it any less the way to go. And if my player doesn't like this and argue any other way I'll point him towards the many ways he have to remove this particular feeding modifier, or tell him to create a character with other feeding hobbies.<br /> <br /> This is the World of Darkness, a gothic-horror role-playing game. Trying to be the good guy is supposed to be hard and difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T21:55:16-07:00","id":587702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587566#post587566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I'm going to reassert a previous challenge:<br /> Cite the revised preview texts. You keep asserting things about both Hunger and Tyrants, but I really am not seeing this in the text as it stands.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587578#post587578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no proof that its non-viable. I agree with the above - got quotes to back up your claims?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. I apologize if there is too much cited text in what follows -- mods: please notify me and I will remove whatever material needs removing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunger for Power - Revised Version (03 Beast Chapter One)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tyrants are Beasts who crave power, feeding off the act of besting someone and proving their own superiority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 1 - Besting and proving superiority is suggested as ways that Tyrants can feed. The Sub has already surrendered. At most there might be some brat taming. There is nothing to best and no way to prove your superiority.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunger for Power - Revised Version (03 Beast Chapter One)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They bask in the fear, respect, and trembling worship of those beneath them, whether the Beast is standing at the top of the pyramid or controlling things from the shadows while their subjects tremble at the thought of their unseen king.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 2 - Fear, respect, and trembling worship are suggested as ways that Tyrants can feed. There might be fear in the Sub; fear that you will go too far or hurt them too badly or not provide adequate after care. But this is not the level of fear that seems to be implied by any of the quotes that I am using.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunger for Power - Revised Version (03 Beast Chapter One)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">a Tyrant thrills in reminding those below him just how powerless tiny mortals really are against the stuff of nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 3 - Further reinforces the themes of defeat and loss of power. The Sub can end everything with a single word. The Sub has the most important power.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunger for Power - Revised Version (03 Beast Chapter One)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A corporate Tyrant might feed by orchestrating his own promotion over that of a hated colleague, delighting as he forces his former equal to polish the nameplate on the door of the Beast\u2019s new corner office.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 4 - Further reinforces the themes of defeat and loss of power. It also references humiliation. The defeat and loss are serious setbacks, not even close to the level one might find in most BDSM relationships. But there is some merit to humiliation play counting.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunger for Power - Revised Version (03 Beast Chapter One)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Tyrant lawyer could find herself working in criminal law, feeding from those moments where the opposing attorney realizes he\u2019s lost the case against her superior skill</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 5 - Further reinforces the themes of loss and defeat. Please note that every example we have seen so far has been pretty major. Even the verbiage has been dramatic with things like 'trembling worship' and 'powerless tiny mortals'.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunger for Power - Revised Version (03 Beast Chapter One)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Anakin] often like to get up close and personal with their victims, holding someone down and watching from mere inches away as he realizes he\u2019s been beaten and the fight leaves his eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 6 - Further reinforces the themes of loss and defeat. Implies genuine struggle. Someone lost and becomes powerless.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunger for Power - Revised Version (03 Beast Chapter One)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She destroys them; she knows what they know and she pokes holes in their beliefs and their facts, showing them sides of the topic they never considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 7 - Further use of powerful and dramatic verbiage. Implies excessive verbal force.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunger for Power - Revised Version (03 Beast Chapter One)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The victim of such a Tyrant may not even recognize an intelligent force behind his misery [...] forcefully reminding her victims of how powerless they are in the Beast\u2019s waters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 8 - Further reinforces the themes of loss and defeat. Misery. Powerlessness. More dramatic verbiage. Implies significant scale.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunger for Power - Revised Version (03 Beast Chapter One)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not having the top floor that will make him happy. It\u2019s taking it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 9 - It's not just being dominant and having people beneath him, it's making others lose. Defeating them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Food &amp; Drink - Revised Version (04 Beast Chapter Two)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Horror just wants the Hunger sated in the deepest and most brutal way possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 10 - Excess. VERY dramatic verbiage. Implies scale far greater than most BDSM relationships are willing to take things.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Food &amp; Drink - Revised Version (04 Beast Chapter Two)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Horror has no use for temperance when gluttony is a virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 11 - Same as Article 10.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Food &amp; Drink - Revised Version (04 Beast Chapter Two)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The primordial self doesn\u2019t care what side the Beast chooses, but it can\u2019t abide the middle. It wants rage or contentment. It wants anything but boredom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 12 - Same as Article 10.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 07-12-2015, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T21:58:03-07:00","id":587703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587566#post587566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't even a consistent position. You agree you can feed off of beating someone in a boxing match, but your opponent consented to being there, consented to a set of rules that dictate who the winner is, and so on. But the consent there doesn't matter. The artificial constraints don't matter. You can win and feed.</div> </div> </div> </div>But your opponent did not agree to lose the match before they even got into the ring. That's the difference for me.<br /> You didn't take it. They gave it to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 07-12-2015, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T22:01:36-07:00","id":587704,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how that penalty applies. On a purely semantic level, it seems a bad call simply because it's so confusing. &quot;My prey brought themselves to me... counts as a -2? Huh?&quot; If my Beast challenges someone to a fight does that get a -2 when they accept to fight? Because they're bringing themselves to me?<br /> <br /> It just seems... desperate to apply a penalty. The controls on this sort of thing are in what it takes to satisfy the requirements for a feeding at higher Satiety levels. The examples of low Satiety options for Power are all things most BDSM play will meet with ease (&quot;Shouting or staring someone down, or just threatening to punch them if they don\u2019t shut up, would also apply.&quot;) While a high Satiety Tyrant simply isn't going to get the kind of power rush described out of BDSM play, because they need power on a completely different scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T22:02:27-07:00","id":587706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587702#post587702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright. I apologize if there is too much cited text in what follows -- mods: please notify me and I will remove whatever material needs removing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The complete text is available for anyone to read for free on the kickstarter page. I honestly wouldn't worry about quoting too much of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:04:30-07:00","id":587891,"title":"","content":"Incendax, that was a very handy way of addressing that. Thank you for your time investment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T01:19:08-07:00","id":587919,"title":"","content":"There is one circumstance I could see it working without moving into the abusive territory. I'll prephase this wit the fact that I barely remember this since it was hardly relevant to me at the time and there's about a decade between then and now. Anyway I vaguely remember an episode of a show on TechTv years back called &quot;Unscrewed&quot; where they had these guests who were wrestling doms or something like that. Essentially they worked with people who wanted to submit to someone, but the fantasy required that sub actually has the power taken from them as opposed to just handing it over. <br /> <br /> While it certainly wouldn't work for higher levels of satiety I think it could work at the lower levels. Just play the aspect as the clientele are expected to give the struggle their all before they submit and I think it might work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T02:24:54-07:00","id":587973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587702#post587702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Article 1 - Besting and proving superiority is suggested as ways that Tyrants can feed. The Sub has already surrendered. At most there might be some brat taming. There is nothing to best and no way to prove your superiority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Article 1 fails.<br /> <br /> Proving superiority are stated in the text is not incompatible with BDSM. The feeding options for low Satiety Hunger of Power including simply threatening someone and getting them to shut up. Exerting your control over someone you already have bested/gained dominance over is completely in line with the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Article 2 - Fear, respect, and trembling worship are suggested as ways that Tyrants can feed. There might be fear in the Sub; fear that you will go too far or hurt them too badly or not provide adequate after care. But this is not the level of fear that seems to be implied by any of the quotes that I am using. </div> </div> </div>Article 2 fails.<br /> <br /> The unstated assumption for your statement is that the emotions felt during BDSM play are either fake, or real but don't count for a reason nothing here establishes. A dominant partner that creates actual fear in their submissive in the headspace of a scene has created fear. Tyrants can feed off of fear. Without demonstrating why this fear doesn't count in the text, this doesn't hold. Shifting to other fears is missing the point.<br /> <br /> You aslo don't address respect, or worship. A large number of BDSM practices revolve around having subs demonstrate their true feelings of towards their dominant partner. These are also emotions where the whole &quot;I can call red&quot; part doesn't really matter. A submissive partner generally doesn't just respect their dominant partner for a scene. The scene simply provides a demonstration of that respect; and for a Tyrant would be a chance to bask in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Article 3 - Further reinforces the themes of defeat and loss of power. The Sub can end everything with a single word. The Sub has the most important power. </div> </div> </div>Article 3 fails.<br /> <br /> You're conflating the Horror and the Tyrant. The Horror being fed doesn't care if the target could stop things. It cares if it is feed its emotional food. If a Tyrant makes a submissive feel powerless and small, the Horror is sated. The fact that the sub could stop it doesn't matter to whether or not feeding is possible. It would only matter if feeding happens in that specific case (just like all feeding since no feeding is without a risk that you don't actually provoke an emotional response successfully).<br /> <br /> The Tyrant's desire to thrill in the act is also not dependent on the subs ability to remove consent. Dominants thrill in the act IRL BDSM.<br /> <br /> This reads like you're trying to use one to prop up the other.<br /> <br /> As well &quot;themes&quot; are extremely broad, and extreme vague concepts. You aren't really using the term in a specific sense, so it adds little clarity, or robustness to your position. Chopping up paragraphs into single sentences to call them multiple Articles doesn't help either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Article 4 - Further reinforces the themes of defeat and loss of power. It also references humiliation. The defeat and loss are serious setbacks, not even close to the level one might find in most BDSM relationships. But there is some merit to humiliation play counting. </div> </div> </div>Article 4 is mostly Article 3 again.<br /> <br /> The analysis continues to miss the issue of the requisite amount of effort that goes into feeding is Satiety relevant. How much you have to feed the Horror is not constant. Getting a promotion is listed as a Moderate Satiety level feeding, which means there are less involved Low Satiety level feeding options around. The seriousness of a setback for the target is not what says if it can be used for feeding at all. How sated the Horror is dictates how serious the impact on the target has to be to work. A high Satiety Tyrant wouldn't find their Horror satisfied with either humiliation play, or dicking over a rival for a promotion sufficient for their Horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Article 5 - Further reinforces the themes of loss and defeat. Please note that every example we have seen so far has been pretty major. Even the verbiage has been dramatic with things like 'trembling worship' and 'powerless tiny mortals'. </div> </div> </div>I think you're overly conflating &quot;proving superiority&quot; with &quot;themes of loss and defeat.&quot; This only really works when you're breaking these up like this, instead of the overall context of the section in question.<br /> <br /> And no, every example we have seens so far as not been pretty major. You skipped physically roughing up a drunk and getting them to beg for their life, which is a powerful moment, but not really a major one. The lawyer example doesn't really seem fairly major. To their clients maybe, but to the lawyers it is just another case. There's no significant loss for the actual target (the other lawyer). Lawyers win and lose all the time. The text doesn't explicitly state this is busting another lawyer's perfect streak. Just showing the Tyrant is the better lawyer. We don't know if the Tyrant is a defense attorney that helped a nobody get off a first time pot possession, or a DA sending a mob boss to jail for life; because those details are irrelevant. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Article 6 - Further reinforces the themes of loss and defeat. Implies genuine struggle. Someone lost and becomes powerless. </div> </div> </div>Article 6 fails.<br /> <br /> There's no loss, just defeat. There's no statement of &quot;genuine&quot; struggle on the behalf of the victim (esp. in the light of many of the examples after this passage where the victims never actually have a chance to struggle). It just says they like to make it personal and let their victims know it was them. It also doesn't say, &quot;lost and powerless,&quot; it says that they realize they've been beaten, and have lost the will to fight back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Article 7 - Further use of powerful and dramatic verbiage. Implies excessive verbal force.<br /> Article 8 - Further reinforces the themes of loss and defeat. Misery. Powerlessness. More dramatic verbiage. Implies significant scale.<br /> Article 9 - It's not just being dominant and having people beneath him, it's making others lose. Defeating them. </div> </div> </div>All of these are snipped so far out of context it's ridiculous. These are all sample characters, and your interpretations of them seem like cherry picked sentences desperate for a point.<br /> <br /> Article 7 is about a female Tyrant that feeds by <b>aggressively winning arguments</b>. Excessive verbal force... is supposed to prove BDSM doesn't count? How?<br /> Article 8 is chopped up to hell, and noticeably skipping right over the word &quot;subtle&quot; also being part of the verbiage.<br /> Article 9 as doesn't show your interpretation at all. Dave's whole write up says nothing about making others lose or defeating people. He wants to take the positions of power. That's it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Article 10 - Excess. VERY dramatic verbiage. Implies scale far greater than most BDSM relationships are willing to take things.<br /> Article 11 - Same as Article 10.<br /> Article 12 - Same as Article 10. </div> </div> </div>Article 10 is contradictory.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dramatic verbiage&quot; is getting old to the point of having no meaning. It's a purely subjective thing being tossed around like something you can tick off and it amounts to more than that if you get enough ticks gathered. If anything it's the opposite of scale. The Horror doesn't care lessons or teaching or artistry in the hunt. It wants feed. It doesn't care if the victim is willing or not. It cares that the victim is made to feel. If a dominant Tyrant pulls their submissive aside, negotiates a &quot;I'm going to beat you until you red&quot; scene, it can be brutal, and quick. It's perfectly in line with the text here, which is not in line with any implications about greater scale.<br /> <br /> Article 11 fails with 10.<br /> <br /> Also, it is again suffering for cherry picking. The whole point of that passage is that the needs of the Hunger change with Satiety. A hunger Horror just wants food now. A Horror that's being feed wants better food; not just more food. It is a glutton that doesn't want to keep feeding on the same thing over and over. Stealing a gold watch might be enough when it's starving, but when it's had its appetizer, it wants gold that matters far more than that. For a Tyrant, that gets right back to the point that BDSM might not work for all levels of Satiety, but that doesn't mean it doesn't work at all. Your looking for all the examples that line up to upper Moderate and High Satiety feeding issues and treating Low and lower Moderate Satiety feeding as if they don't exist.<br /> <br /> <br /> Article 12 is actually not the same as 10 and 11. It is, however, irrelevant. It's talking about how Horrors don't like the middle level of Satiety. It has nothing to do with scale, or what counts for feeding. All this does is further the impression you're not putting any of these statements in their context, but rather looking for collections of words that might support your position.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But your opponent did not agree to lose the match before they even got into the ring. That's the difference for me.<br /> You didn't take it. They gave it to you. </div> </div> </div>Your opponent agreed on the parameters of the match, including what counts as losing, and concedes when that condition is met. The only difference you've shown is that you consider getting punch in a fight is real enough, but getting punched in a BDSM scene isn't.<br /> <br /> And in all twelve examples, you never give a single example that supports that the target giving their submission matters to a Tyrant.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T02:28:30-07:00","id":587975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=587919#post587919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially they worked with people who wanted to submit to someone, but the fantasy required that sub actually has the power taken from them as opposed to just handing it over.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fairly common thing in lots of BDSM play. It's pretty much the core of all consensual non-consent play, where the negotiated parameters of the scene include actively removing power in various forms from the sub.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T03:40:55-07:00","id":588003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_conta