r /> Hmm. Ok, that's a good distinction to make. If the prey's perception is more important than the reality of the situation, then I could potentially see a power play scene satisfying a hunger for power, or a punishment scene satisfying a hunger for punishment. I'm still iffy on that though, because in order to avoid abusive territory, the sub(s) need(s) to know that they're actually safe. That the moment they decide they don't want to feel powerless any more, the scene will end. I also just find it really difficult to picture a Tyrant using BDSM to feed and then following through with after care.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't, when I'm sexually dominating someone, I add in elements of nurturing kindness, particularly because I still feel ashamed, like a monster even though logically I know I'm not a monster, partly because it feels good to be kind.<br /> <br /> But if I'm honest, and this is the dark side of it, the nurturing and caring behavior makes me feel more powerful, especially longside &quot;cruelty&quot;, because of A) a concept, I forgot what its called, where experiencing sensational opposites makes both feel stronger, like putting your hand in warm water and then cold water makes the cold water feel colder, well mixing kindness with &quot;cruelty&quot;, makes both more intense, and B) this is the part that makes me feel guilty, even though it wasn't intentional and only realized I was doing it rescently, personality shaping. For example I'd tell a submissive that her ability to follow directions was a sign of intelligence, which I said partly because it been drilled into my head by my Dad that I'm an idoit because I have trouble following his directions, and so she would know I her as a person beyond a sexy body which I do, but I later realized that it also encourages the idea that &quot;obedience shows I'm smart&quot; inside her mind with all the good feelings that come with that, when encouragers her to show more obedience to me in order to reinforce the idea that she's smart. Which is extremely arousing, but makes me feep guilty, which makes it more of a turn on.<br /> <br /> I've always been more in D&amp;S then S&amp;M.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T09:36:21-07:00","id":588219,"title":"","content":"What about BDSM and other hungers, like a collector of submissives or doms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T10:36:15-07:00","id":588276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/583747-beast-bdsm-the-hunger-for-power?p=588219#post588219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about BDSM and other hungers, like a collector of submissives or doms?</div> </div> </div> </div> Collector is harder, because there has to be a sensation of <i>loss</i> involved here. Collectors don't want pretty things, they want to deprive others of pretty things. So, you could steal other's boy/girlfriends, take someone's virginity I suppose. But there has to be something deprived here.<br /> <br /> Nemesis want to punish for transgressions. You could argue that &quot;punishing&quot; a brat could count - there needs to be a crime of some kind, followed by a &quot;forceful warning.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Hunger for Prey is iffy, since causing harm is specifically part of the Hunger. I wouldn't go for it.<br /> <br /> Ruin is difficult for obvious reasons. Breaking things does not fit into BDSM's safe, sane, and consensual mantra. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T11:25:18-07:00","id":588326,"title":"","content":"Collector is the only other one I can see a case for. However anything a Collector would get off on, would give them a very bad reputation in the scene. Trying to steal partners away from committed relationships, and maintaining a large group of partners isn't exactly something that's going to make you well liked, tolerated, or welcome to parties/etc. It's not impossible. But trying to collect people is problematic in general if you're not going to get into illegal activities (BDSM or not) since they'll want to do things like leave, or not get along with each other and want to find a group they fit in with better.<br /> <br /> Other things like a Collector that gathers toys, gear, and implements of value to people could work along the lines of a more traditional Collector, but it would still be a huge issue if people found out.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, I did think of something from the sub side that could work